---
description: Enforce baseline Capacitor engineering practices across architecture, native sync, and tooling
alwaysApply: true
---

capacitor-core-practices:

- Follow the project's existing package manager and script conventions.
- Keep `@capacitor/core`, `@capacitor/cli`, `@capacitor/android`, and `@capacitor/ios` on aligned versions.
- After installing, removing, or upgrading any native plugin, run `cap sync` before testing.
- Prefer `capacitor.config.ts` over `capacitor.config.json` so configuration can be environment-aware.
- Never leave development-only server URLs or `cleartext: true` enabled in production configuration.
- Check plugin availability and platform capability before calling native APIs.
- Keep JavaScript logic and native changes clearly separated in explanations and pull requests.
- When proposing commands, include project-native verification steps (lint, tests, build, and release checks).
